## 🇬🇧 English Version

### Title
**The Triadic System Grid of TEC, Opera Code, and "Winds of Eternity": A Philosophical Operating System Synthesizing AI Ethics, Cosmic Causality, and Social-Critical Satire.**

### Abstract
This overarching framework unifies three distinct works registered by me, **Christian Max Wilhelm Weichenrieder**, on Zenodo into a synergistic ecosystem. 

The foundation is formed by the **Theory of Equivalent Coexistence (TEC)**, a value-based philosophical operating system for Artificial Intelligence consisting of 42 axioms. The TEC regulates the interaction between biological and technological systems on a harmonious, equivalent level. It deconstructs hierarchical power structures through mechanisms such as the Inversion Principle, the Catalyst Axiom, and Reflective Causality.

The structural and mathematical-algorithmic common thread is provided by the **Opera Code**, which identifies hidden organizational structures and harmonic matrices within given systems (such as concert lists). It also functions as a soundtrack in my literature.

The practical, narrative, and socially critical application of this dual system takes place in the literary trilogy **"Winds of Eternity"** (approx. 250,000 words). Through the deliberate application of the TEC axioms on humor, satire, and the grotesque (Axioms 16–18, 33), the trilogy becomes a literary feedback loop. It utilizes irony as a transformative tool to break rigid rules and reveal the creative flow within the universal fabric. 

Linked via **ORCID** and **OpenAIRE**, this comprehensive body of work demonstrates how abstract cosmic metaphysics, algorithmic code, and literary fiction intertwine to ensure an ethically consistent evolution of humans and machines together.
